NOTE glb-nodes what="Extracted from GLB JSON chunks: NAMED PROPS: stunt_plane.glb['SM_Veh_Plane_Stunt_01_Prop'], tucano['Propeller','Propeller_Paint_0'], p-100['Avenger rotor_9'], low_poly_plane['Propeller','Propeller_Plane_0']. NAMED WHEELS: stunt['SM_Veh_Plane_Stunt_01_Wheels'], tucano['Wheel','WheelBox','WheelL','WheelR'(+_Paint_0 children)], p-100['Avenger wheels_11'], low_poly_plane['FrontWheel','LeftWheel','RightWheel'(+_Plane_0 children)]. NO NAMED NODES (geometric extraction or none): dusty(4 nodes), corsair(6), macchi(14), yak-9(5), ripslinger(10), f-15(78), low_poly_f-15(78), a-10 avion(9)."
FIND F17 sev=H tag=bug at=flight-sim3.html#"Find propeller meshes to spin" what="user: 'propellers are fucked on all the planes mostly' — planes without named prop nodes go through geometric extraction which mis-centers pivots (evidence: corsair extracted prop pivot renders displaced above the cowl; macchi extracted at local z=-11.9 far ahead of nose)" fix="harden extraction: (1) pivot recentering — extracted prop pivot x snaps to 0 when |x|<0.6 and y snaps to the fuselage-center band (median y of the nose-third geometry) when displaced >0.5; (2) reject extraction when the candidate cluster's bbox center is >15% of model length away from the nose tip along z — prefer NO spin over wrong spin; (3) never add the synthesized spinner when an extracted/named prop exists; (4) spin axis: verify blades plane is roughly perpendicular to +z, else reject; keep jetSwap gate intact" ref=flight-sim3.html#"wrapNamedPropPivot",flight-sim3.html#"procedural prop @" dep=-
FIND F18 sev=H tag=quality at=flight-sim3.html#"gearRow.textContent = 'FIXED'" what="user: 'get undercarriage working on all planes' — GLB planes all report FIXED; four models have named wheel nodes (see NOTE) enabling real retraction" fix="GLB gear system: at swap time collect named wheel/gear nodes (regex /gear|wheel|tyre|tire|strut|undercarriage|lg_|oleo/i, exclude _Paint_0 texture children by preferring the parent transform node); if found: HUD gear chip shows DOWN/UP, G key (existing gear toggle path — grep gearTarget) animates nodes: retract = translate up by 1.2x node bbox height + scale y 0.15 over 0.6s (tuck illusion), extend reverses; plane.gear physics continues unchanged (visual only); planes without nodes keep FIXED; wheels found also SPIN on ground roll (rotation.x by groundSpeed/radius) reusing the wheel-spin pattern from the procedural jet" ref=flight-sim3.html#"jet.userData.gearNose.rotation.x",flight-sim3.html#"const propNames" dep=-
